   "label": "f02-version-relational",
   "front": "What replaces the in-memory expectedVersion check on a relational database?",
   "back": "A concurrency token (RowVersion or IsConcurrencyToken) so UPDATE ... WHERE Version = @expected hits 0 rows on a stale write and EF raises DbUpdateConcurrencyException (HTTP 409/412); or ExecuteUpdateAsync with a version Where and 0 affected rows meaning someone else got there first.",
   "observation": "read-derived",
